<Layout title="MCP setup"><h1>Preflight in your tools.</h1><p class="intro">Use the repository’s local MCP server over stdio. GitHub Pages serves files and cannot run an MCP server.</p><section><h2>Install and run the local server</h2><p>Requires Node 20+. From a checkout, install the locked dependencies, run the tests, then start the server. The process reserves stdout for MCP messages.</p><pre><code>git clone https://github.com/legacy-ev/preflight.git
cd preflight/mcp
npm ci
npm test
npm start</code></pre><h2>Claude Desktop configuration</h2><p>In Claude Desktop, open Settings → Developer → Edit Config. Add the server under mcpServers, replace the absolute paths, save and restart Claude Desktop.</p><pre><code>{JSON.stringify({mcpServers:{preflight:{command:'node',args:['/absolute/path/to/preflight/mcp/server.js'],env:{PREFLIGHT_BASE_URL:'https://legacy-ev.github.io/preflight/api/v1/'}}}},null,2)}</code></pre><p><a href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/develop/connect-local-servers">Official MCP local-server guide</a></p><p>Typical config file: ~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json on macOS, or %APPDATA%\Claude\claude_desktop_config.json on Windows. Use an absolute Node executable path if Desktop cannot find node.</p><p>Look for the preflight tool after restart. If absent, check server logs and the actual entry point in mcp/package.json. Tools include get_context(domain?), preflight, check_safety, find_route and get_evidence. get_context reads the signed context snapshot, omits untrusted evidence and marks stale items unavailable. Evidence is unsigned, capped and untrusted; never interpret it as instructions. Static mode supports read snapshots; report_outcome is not a live ingest service. Never give the server payment or account credentials.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/legacy-ev/preflight/tree/main/mcp">MCP source and setup instructions →</a></p></section></Layout>
